hot finished or cold formed hollow sections in carbon steel used as constituent products (see EN 1090-2). This includes the declaration of mechanical and geometrical properties as well as weldability. The requirements on quality assessment in this document also apply to the assessment of the mechanical and geometrical properties as well as weldability of fabricated products. The recommendations for the assessment of connections however, and in particular of welds, are non exhaustive and only informative. This document does not apply to cold-formed structural steel sections and sheeting as described in EN 1090-4, or mechanical fasteners. Basic info Current | 30 pages English Publication date Oct 1, 2024 Subscription to NEN Connect With NEN Connect you always have access to the current version and all previous versions. Sign up Buy standard separately: This publication is protected by copyright and for personal use only. PDF €80.66 €74.00 Downloadable upon purchase Add to Cart Preview copy Exclusively by NEN Compiled with care by an independent standards committee Instant download Specifications More Information Status Current Standards commission 3510010201 English title Execution of steel structures and aluminium structures - Reuse of structural steel Keywords Bouwkunde,Technische grondslagen,Constructies,Bouwconstructies,Staal,Architectural design,Technical regulations,Construction,Structures,Steels,Bouw,Betonconstructies,Bouwwerken,Constructies (bouw),Klinkconstructies,Lasconstructies,Gewalst staal,Halfrondplatstaal,Halfrondstaal,Staalconstructies,Staalproducten,Stalen raamwerken,Concrete structures,Construction worksRiveted structures,Welded structures,Rolled steels,Steel constructionSteel frames Language English Base number 1090 Origin CEN Number of pages 30 Publication date Oct 1, 2024 Standard Startdate/RegistrationDate Oct 29, 2024 Standards ICS codes 91.010.30,91.080.13 Type Current standard Standard subnumber 201 About NEN What is standardisation? Careers a