  "https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/projects/crclr-house-berlin/": {
    "url": "https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/projects/crclr-house-berlin/",
    "fetched": true,
    "http_status": "200",
    "text": "CRCLR House - Building Social Ecology Skip to content Building Social Ecology Start Patterns Projects Theory About en de CRCLR House: is a centre for circular economy practices in the sectors of construction, living and community. The CRCLR House is being built in a section of the former Kindl brewery in Berlin Neukölln. The existing warehouse is being extended by a modular wooden panel construction, so that the building can accommodate residential and commercial uses. The aim is to create living, working and commercial spaces in which materials are recycled in accordance with the principles of the Circular Economy. Likewise, during construction, attention will be paid to the recyclability of materials, or secondary building materials will be used and disassembly strategies will be considered. For example, resources were conserved by installing second-hand windows. As part of the initial use, the existing building was made usable again with only a few interventions and was available for temporary use as an event venue, coworking space and artist studio for the CRCLR community. As soon as the building is finalized, the Impact Hub Berlin will move in and offer co-working spaces, lab facilities and an event program. Workshop on the construction site © Marlene Hildebrandt Under construction © Marlene Hildebrandt Entrance and original façade of the CRCLR House © Michael Prytula Reusable façade elements © Marlene Hildebrandt The hall before the reconstruction © Chantal Schöpp Second level in the existing building during the reconstruction © Marlene Hildebrandt In the hall during the reconstruction © Marlene Hildebrandt General information Architects Die Zusammenarbeiter GmbH ﻿ ﻿ Owner TRNSFRM eG ﻿ ﻿ Address Rollbergstraße 26, 12053 Berlin ﻿ ﻿ Construction period 2019 – now (2021) ﻿ ﻿ Construction former warehouse is upgraded and supplemented with a timber construction ﻿ ﻿ Residents / Space BGF 6600 m 2 , living area 2.525 m², commercial area 2.346 m² Sources 