    "text": "Willmott Dixon - Fore Partnership - Case Study - Qualisflow Skip to content Home Solutions Materials Quality Waste Qflow for Contractors Qflow for Developers Qflow For BREEAM Certification Integrations Resource Hub Case Studies Blog The State of Data Quality in Construction Report UK Construction Waste Report Carbon Assessment 2025 Company About Careers News Contact Contact Sales Contact Support Sign in Book a Demo Menu Close Home Solutions Materials Quality Waste Qflow for Contractors Qflow for Developers Qflow For BREEAM Certification Integrations Resource Hub Case Studies Blog The State of Data Quality in Construction Report UK Construction Waste Report Carbon Assessment 2025 Company About Careers News Contact Contact Sales Contact Support Sign in Book a Demo Willmott Dixon & FORE - TBC.London Willmott Dixon, one of UK’s leading independent construction and property services company used Qflow on site to log every material delivery and waste transfer through a simple photograph of the delivery slip. Introduction TBC.London is one of London’s first net zero carbon in operation workplaces. FORE appointed Willmott Dixon as the principal contractor and Stiff+Trevillion as lead architects. By deploying Qflow on site to log every material delivery and waste transfer through a simple photograph. This allowed Willmott Dixon to save time, and identify non-compliant deliveries and incomplete documentation. 180 hours saved 100% FSC compliant < 265 kg CO2e/m2 verified The Challenge Manually tracking and auditing waste and materials was time consuming and opaque. “Qflow enables our teams to work smarter, not harder.” – Ketan Dalvi, Willmott Dixon, Senior Sustainability Manager The Solution Automated data capture and auditing Willmott Dixon used Qflow to streamline logging material deliveries and waste transfers through simple photographs of delivery slips. Qflow’s AI digitised and audited this data, alerting the team to non-compliant deliveries and incomplete documentation, saving over 2 hours per week on manual data entry and 22 working days over the project’s duration. This replaced unreliable spreadsheets, improving accuracy. Qflow also centralised sustainability reporting by automating waste data input and compliance checks, allowing the site team to focus on core tasks. Its user-friendly dashboard provided transparency at the client level, showing project status against design estimates and quickly flagging missing information. Download the full case study below to learn more about how Willmott Dixon achieved this and the plans for future sustainable developments! Download full Case Study Speak with our expert sales team to book a demo Enabling responsible, resource efficient construction; cutting waste and carbon. Qflow automates on site data capture and auditing, feeding it into your existing tools Book a demo Get your free sustainability score today Take our 2-minute quiz and we’ll send you a free report showing your sustainability readiness and what you can do to track, measure and reduce as-build project carbon Take our sustainability quiz About us Qflow is a data platform that captures real-time materials and waste information at the source, enabling project teams to make informed decisions on cost, carbon, and quality. Linkedin Solutions Qflow for Contractors Qflow for Developers Integrations Find us REGISTERED OFFICE UK Qualis Flow, FR.108, Workspace – The Frames, 1 Phipp Street, London, EC2A 4PS REGISTERED OFFICE US 98 Cuttermill Road #466, Great Neck, NY 11021  Support Our support team is on-hand to help between 9 AM – 5:30 PM GMT. support@qualisflow.com © Copyright 2025. Qualis Flow Ltd. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy | Sitemap",
